---
import Content from "../Content.astro";
import SectionHead from "../Section.astro";
import ProjectPubs from "../../layouts/ProjectPubs.astro";
import PubButton from "../buttons/PubButton.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import teacherMB from "../../assets/img/teacher-MB.jpg";
import fieldwork from "../../assets/img/fieldwork.png";
import teacherTooth from "../../assets/img/teacher-tooth.png";
import cntl from "cntl";

const firstParagraphClasses = cntl`
  first-letter:text-8xl
  first-letter:font-semibold
  first-letter:mr-2
  first-letter:float-left
`;

const spaceClasses = cntl`mr-1`;
---

<div>
  <SectionHead
    title="Education & Broader Impacts"
    subtitle="Connecting scientific research with educators, students, and communities across Florida"
  />
  <Content>
    <p class={firstParagraphClasses}>
      Science is most powerful when it is accessible. As the coordinator for the
      <a href="https://www.floridamuseum.ufl.edu/earth-systems/scientist-in-every-florida-school/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-porsche-300 hover:text-porsche-200 underline underline-offset-2">Scientist in Every Florida School (SEFS)</a>
      program at the University of Florida Thompson Earth Systems Institute and Florida Museum of Natural
      History, I develop and manage programs that place scientists directly into
      K-12 classrooms and build lasting partnerships between researchers and
      educators. This work spans teacher professional development, research-based
      curriculum design, scientist-classroom partnerships, and outreach
      programming that expands access to Earth and environmental sciences across
      Florida — particularly in underserved and rural communities. Since 2019,
      I have spearheaded, implemented, managed, and coordinated over 20 professional
      development programs connecting K-12 teachers with cutting-edge research
      across paleontology, AI, ecology, plant biology, and environmental science.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-porsche-950/20 dark:border-porsche-50/20">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-porsche-300 mb-3">Montbrook Teacher Field Experiences</h3>
      <p class="mt-2">
        One of SEFS's most powerful teacher professional development experiences takes place at the
        <a href="https://www.floridamuseum.ufl.edu/montbrook/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-porsche-300 hover:text-porsche-200 underline underline-offset-2">Montbrook fossil site</a>
        in Levy County, Florida — one of the most productive late Miocene vertebrate fossil localities
        in the southeastern United States. Teachers participate in authentic paleontological fieldwork
        alongside museum scientists, excavating and identifying fossil specimens in the field. This
        immersive experience is designed to give teachers firsthand exposure to scientific methods,
        helping them bring the nature of science to life in their own classrooms. Lessons developed
        around this experience connect fossil collection, stratigraphic context, and evolutionary
        history directly to K-12 science standards.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
        <figure>
          <Image
            src={teacherMB}
            alt="Teachers at the Montbrook fossil site holding orange SEFS tote bags after a professional development dig experience"
            width={400}
            class="rounded-xl w-full object-cover"
          />
          <figcaption class="text-xs text-porsche-950 dark:text-porsche-50 mt-2 pl-3 border-l-2 border-porsche-950 dark:border-porsche-50 leading-relaxed">
            Teachers at the Montbrook fossil site following a SEFS professional development dig experience.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <Image
            src={fieldwork}
            alt="Scientists and teachers excavating fossils in the field at Montbrook"
            width={400}
            class="rounded-xl w-full object-cover"
          />
          <figcaption class="text-xs text-porsche-950 dark:text-porsche-50 mt-2 pl-3 border-l-2 border-porsche-950 dark:border-porsche-50 leading-relaxed">
            Hands-on fossil excavation during the Montbrook teacher field experience.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <Image
            src={teacherTooth}
            alt="Teacher holding a fossil tooth found during the Montbrook dig"
            width={400}
            class="rounded-xl w-full object-cover"
          />
          <figcaption class="text-xs text-porsche-950 dark:text-porsche-50 mt-2 pl-3 border-l-2 border-porsche-950 dark:border-porsche-50 leading-relaxed">
            A teacher displays a fossil tooth recovered during fieldwork at Montbrook.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-porsche-950/20 dark:border-porsche-50/20">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-porsche-300 mb-3">Professional Development Initiatives</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 mb-4">
        Below is a selection of teacher professional development programs I have led through
        <a href="https://www.floridamuseum.ufl.edu/earth-systems/scientist-in-every-florida-school/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-porsche-300 hover:text-porsche-200 underline underline-offset-2">SEFS</a>,
        spanning paleontology, AI and machine learning, ecology, plant biology, and environmental science.
      </p>
      <div class="text-sm text-porsche-950 dark:text-porsche-50 space-y-2">
        <div class="border-l-2 border-porsche-300 pl-3 py-1">
          <span class="font-semibold">2026–2027</span> — Modeling Human Behavior in Climate Disasters Using Artificial Intelligence <span class="text-porsche-950/60 dark:text-porsche-50/60">(with X. Zhao)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-porsche-300 pl-3 py-1">
          <span class="font-semibold">2026–2027</span> — Experimental Design Using Robotic Fish <span class="text-porsche-950/60 dark:text-porsche-50/60">(with P. Musgrave)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-porsche-300 pl-3 py-1">
          <span class="font-semibold">2026–2027</span> — Archaeological Exploration of the Jupiter Inlet <span class="text-porsche-950/60 dark:text-porsche-50/60">(with A. Neilson)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-porsche-300 pl-3 py-1">
          <span class="font-semibold">2026</span> — Chewing on Change: Using Machine Learning to Assess Variation in Fossilized Horse Teeth <span class="text-porsche-950/60 dark:text-porsche-50/60">(with A. Neilson & C. Wusylko)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-porsche-300 pl-3 py-1">
          <span class="font-semibold">2025</span> — Ecological Competition Between Invasive and Native Species <span class="text-porsche-950/60 dark:text-porsche-50/60">(with B. Xue & M. Leibold)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-porsche-300 pl-3 py-1">
          <span class="font-semibold">2025–2028</span> — BII: Polyploidy: Integration Across Scales and Biological Systems <span class="text-porsche-950/60 dark:text-porsche-50/60">(with P. & D. Soltis)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-porsche-300 pl-3 py-1">
          <span class="font-semibold">2023–2024</span> — Research Infrastructure: Moving and Improving the Florida Museum Fish Collection <span class="text-porsche-950/60 dark:text-porsche-50/60">(with M. Ennes)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-porsche-300 pl-3 py-1">
          <span class="font-semibold">2022–2025</span> — SEFS Cohorts I–IV: AI Learning in K-12 with Fossil Sharks <span class="text-porsche-950/60 dark:text-porsche-50/60">(with B. Abramowitz, B. MacFadden, P. Antonenko & J. Waisome)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-porsche-300 pl-3 py-1">
          <span class="font-semibold">2022–2025</span> — SEFS Cohorts I–IV: Plant Pathology Professional Development for High School Teachers <span class="text-porsche-950/60 dark:text-porsche-50/60">(with W. Y. Song)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-porsche-300 pl-3 py-1">
          <span class="font-semibold">2022</span> — Chewing on Change: Bringing Fossil Horses into Title I Schools <span class="text-porsche-950/60 dark:text-porsche-50/60">(with B. Abramowitz, J. Bokor, J. Pirlo & B. MacFadden)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-porsche-300 pl-3 py-1">
          <span class="font-semibold">2022</span> — Adaptations, Evolution, and Climate Change Miami-Dade Teacher PD <span class="text-porsche-950/60 dark:text-porsche-50/60">(with B. Abramowitz, K. Carter & B. MacFadden)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-porsche-300 pl-3 py-1">
          <span class="font-semibold">2021</span> — The Hydrosphere Summer Professional Development for Teachers <span class="text-porsche-950/60 dark:text-porsche-50/60">(with B. Abramowitz)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-porsche-300 pl-3 py-1">
          <span class="font-semibold">2020</span> — The Nature of Science Summer Professional Development for Teachers <span class="text-porsche-950/60 dark:text-porsche-50/60">(with B. Abramowitz)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-porsche-300 pl-3 py-1">
          <span class="font-semibold">2020</span> — World Wetlands January Summit Teacher Professional Development <span class="text-porsche-950/60 dark:text-porsche-50/60">(with B. Abramowitz & B. MacFadden)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-porsche-300 pl-3 py-1">
          <span class="font-semibold">2019</span> — Connections to the Biosphere Summer Professional Development <span class="text-porsche-950/60 dark:text-porsche-50/60">(with B. Abramowitz, J. Pirlo & B. MacFadden)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-porsche-300 pl-3 py-1">
          <span class="font-semibold">2019</span> — SEFS Montbrook Dig Experience Professional Development <span class="text-porsche-950/60 dark:text-porsche-50/60">(with B. Abramowitz, J. Pirlo & B. MacFadden)</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Content>

  <div class="mt-4 mb-2 text-semibold text-lg">Publications:</div>
